title: karr materialize silently deletes and overwrites tracked project files
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`lib/App/karr/BoardStore.pm:232` and `:234-236`. `materialize_to` unconditionally
`DumpFile`s `config.yml` and removes **every** `tasks/*.md` in the target
directory — and the target is the git root, with no prompt, no `--yes` and no
warning.

Reproduced in a repo that has a committed `tasks/deploy-runbook.md` and a
committed `config.yml` of its own:

    karr materialize
    -> Materialized 1 task(s)
    git status --short
     M config.yml
     D tasks/deploy-runbook.md

`tasks/` and `config.yml` at repo root are not unusual names for a project to
already use. Worse, `karr init` has by then added both paths to `.gitignore`, so
the deletion is hidden from a later `git add` and the user may not notice until
the files are needed.

Fix direction: refuse to materialize into a directory whose `tasks/*.md` or
`config.yml` are tracked by git or were not written by karr, unless an explicit
`--force`/`--yes` is given. At minimum, do not delete files karr did not create.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
